  "id": 203717208797527,
  "uuid": "614db108-62cd-47a8-a6ed-7692555d436d",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "69b3074e-df5f-8877-18c2-238e228075bc",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "13bfe623-202b-f603-acab-b9b8e020f692",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "On the 23rd of February 2019, we held the opening\nceremony for the very first simulation-based competition in Pakistan at the\nCentre for Innovation in Medical Education, Aga Khan University. An idea which\nbegun as an impetus to connect a highly talented and competitive body of staff\nand students to the power of simulation and conflict. To challenge them in ways\nthat would not have been practical just a few years ago. And inspired by what\nother had done around the world, we held our very own SIMWARS. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Our multi-faceted team of organisers consisted of CIME team,\nSPIE (Society for Promotion of Innovation in Education) volunteers, medical\n& nursing students, all of whom were dedicated to bringing a new experience\nto AKU. A new way of sparking thought and creativity in yet uncharted\nterritory. And, now that we've had this event, I'd like to reflect back and to\nplan ahead. What made this event unique? What did it bring to our teams? What\nis the emergent role of simulation in healthcare and how can this event build\non that utility?",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Let's start with the teams. Each included a nurse, a doctor,\nand students from both nursing and medicine. Each team acting as a functional\nunit of the healthcare system. At each stage our participants were faced with controlled\nadversity. We challenged their speed of response, their sheer creativity, the\nsum of their knowledge, their ability to prioritise and yet remain organised, but\nmost importantly their strength in communication.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "All this brouhaha is found in every ward and triage around\nthe world. But, what I believe SIMWARS brought to the table were experiences\nentirely apart from what the walls of the hospital could offer. It acted on a different\ngyrus to the ones we normally use. In one of the more memorable responses to a\nquestion posed by the jury \"Why did you ask the husband for a lighter so you\ncould sanitize the knife?\" the participant - a student - replied, \"I just\nassumed he would as almost everybody smokes these days in Karachi.\" There\nhasn't been a systematic review by Cochrane yet on how many people smoke in\nKarachi, but he was right. The husband had a lighter.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Simulation allows us to learn and see things in new and\nsometimes more practical ways. It gave us, as the organisers, the ability to\ncreate new worlds and scenarios in a few hours. Our participants were able to learn\nhow to deal with critical situations in controlled environments. We've all\nheard how VR is going to change everything, how AI will make us redundant, how\nrobotics will bring surgery into a new era. Simulation encompasses all of these.\nThe world is changing rapidly and the way we learn must adjust equally so. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Perhaps events like SIMWARS are one part of that puzzle.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Regardless, I hope that the competitors found value in the\nevent. And that in the future we can amplify what was great about this first\nstep and build on it.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Written by,",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Muneeb Khan, Medical Student Year III, AKU",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
